  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 14, 'Illustration of how countries can leverage WHO hosted PCMT'. Inside a panel labelled PRODUCT CATALOGUE MANAGEMENT TOOL, a GLOBAL CATALOGUE (global identifier, unit of use, pharmaceutical information such as dosage form, route of administration and strength, trade item information, and manufacturer, country of origin and shelf life) feeds COUNTRY CATALOGUE A and COUNTRY CATALOGUE B, each adding country identifiers and country-specific information such as registration numbers. The arrows are annotated 'Country catalogues to derive common product information from the global catalog'. Country A Users and Country B Users each work in their own catalogue, and the whole sits on WHO INFRASTRUCTURE.",
